// Where your Apple developer team ID comes from.
//
// It used to live in project.pbxproj, which is tracked. Xcode writes it there
// the moment you pick a team, so every pull after that stopped with "your local
// changes would be overwritten by merge" and named a file nobody had edited on
// purpose. A team ID belongs to a Mac, not to a repository.
//
// So it lives in Signing.local.xcconfig instead, which git ignores. The `?`
// below means "include it if it is there": with no such file the build settings
// resolve exactly as they did before — empty, and Xcode asks you for a team
// like it does on any fresh clone. Nothing here is required for the app to
// build on a machine that has never seen it.
//
// setup-mac.sh writes the local file for you the first time it finds a team in
// the project file. To write it by hand:
//
//     echo 'TRUELINE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOURTEAMID' > ios/Signing.local.xcconfig
//
// Your team ID is the ten characters in Xcode → Settings → Accounts, or at
// developer.apple.com → Membership.

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
